readme.text:
- **The canvas is an ordinary workspace file** (`.excalidraw` JSON), so the model can read it with the existing file tools, it goes into Git, and it travels with the project;
- **The agent gets purpose-built draw/read tools**, so it never has to hand-write low-level element JSON;
- **The rendered image comes back as an image content block**, so on its next step the model can *see* what it drew and correct itself;
- **SVG export** lands in the workspace as a deliverable (PNG goes through the attachment service only — see [Known limitations](#known-limitations)).
